+# Changelog
+
+## 1.2.1 — 2026-11-17 · review pass
+
+### Fixed
+- A condition with a single value where a list is expected (`City in "Delhi"`) was matched character by character,
+  and a number there raised inside the job; it is now read as a list of one, in both the Phase B and the reshaping engine.
+- Changing the table selection could leave Phase A *accepted* with a recipe whose step no longer ran; Phase A is now
+  put back in review and Phase B locked.
+- `bucket others` without a keep list, a source table or a top N now answers with a clear message.
+
+### Changed
+- Without a recipe nothing is written for reshaping: Phase A no longer copies every table, and a selection change
+  answers at once again. The Reshape screen then reads Phase A's tables directly, one page at a time.
+- The chat no longer re-reads Phase A's review workbook on every message (`StructurePhase.tables`).
+- `src/agent` passes the type checker (131 errors before) and is part of the CI gate; `Operation` is an explicit union;
+  `PlanTable` describes what the planner needs from a table; the parser's `column()` always returns a column.
+- `IMPROVEMENTS.md`: the single, prioritised list of what is still open.
+
+## 1.2.0 — 2026-11-16 · reshaping moves into Phase A
+
+### Changed
+- **The pipeline is `A → B → C → D`.** Transformations are no longer a fifth phase after D: the recipe is built with
+  *Reshape with agent* on Phase A's review, and Phases B–D check the reshaped tables.
+- Phase B loads tables the recipe changed or created from `phase_a_shaped/` (row ids `<ref>:r<n>`, with
+  `lineage.parquet` back to the source rows); untouched tables are read from Phase A exactly as before.
+- The recipe replays when Phase A runs again, its review workbook is uploaded, or the table selection changes.
+- Reshaping steps that change numbers (aggregate, allocate, net, convert currency, bucket others) need an explicit
+  confirmation, because the checks now run on their result.
+
+### Fixed
+- A rule-based new column (`classify`) was also added to tables that lack the column the rules test.
+
+### Breaking
+- `/api/v1/runs/{id}/phases/T/...` answers 404 `unknown_phase`; the same chat is at `/phases/A/agent/...`.
+- Runs made under the old flow lose their `T` entry on start-up; a `T_recipe.json` is taken over as Phase A's recipe
+  the next time Phase A runs. Final files of a run already finished under the old flow are still served.
+
+## 1.1.0 — 2026-11-12 · production-hardening audit
+
+### Fixed
+- **Security:** Job Contract refs (`inputs[].ref`, `output_prefix`, `cell_edits_ref`) accepted `..` and absolute
+  paths; they are now confined to the storage root.
+- **Data loss:** restarting a phase while the service was at its job limit deleted the phase's results and then
+  refused the restart. The job slot is now reserved first.
+- **Denial of service:** a backtracking pattern in a chat instruction could hold a worker; patterns are now length-
+  and time-limited.
+- Phases C and D passed file descriptions as the phase label: wrong text on the Results page, sentence-long paths
+  in the results zip, and no report marked as the one to download.
+- `rename column X to Y in <table>` put "in <table>" into the new column name.
+
+### Added
+- Security headers (CSP, frame, sniffing, referrer, HSTS), request ids, one error shape, JSON logs.
+- Sign-in lockout per client address.
+- Audit database (`audit.db`): every accepted action and every local-model call. Endpoints `/api/v1/audit`,
+  `/api/v1/audit/llm`. **Schema version 1** (first migration).
+- `/api/v1/metrics` (Prometheus text).
+- Graceful drain on shutdown (`DQ_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_S`).
+- `DQ_ENV`; production refuses to start without a token and a hash key.
+- `DQ_LLM_ALLOWED_HOSTS`: prompts go only to this machine or a named host.
+- Agent: tool registry, guardrails with explicit confirmation for destructive or large changes, conversation
+  memory, one repair attempt, phase limits at planning time, model and prompt version on change-sets.
+- Agent evaluation: 110 cases, CLI, CI gate.
+- Dockerfile, Compose (Caddy + service + isolated Ollama), `.env.example`, CI with security scans and image smoke test.
+- Pinned dependencies with hashes; `pyproject.toml`.
+- Documentation set under `docs/`.
+
+### Changed
+- **API:** `POST /jobs` validates its body (422 on a malformed one) and needs `job_token` with `callback_url`.
+- **API:** applying an elevated change needs `{"confirm": true}` (409 `confirmation_required` otherwise).
+- **API:** validation and HTTP errors use `{"error": {...}}` instead of FastAPI's `{"detail": ...}`.
+- `/docs` and `/redoc` are off; `/openapi.json` remains.
+- Frontend build tools: vite 8, vitest 5 (0 known vulnerabilities).
+- Prompt version `agent-plan/3`: the model is shown only the tools of the current phase.
+
+### Upgrade notes
+- Set `STRUCTURE_HASH_KEY` and `DQ_API_TOKEN` before using `DQ_ENV=production`.
+- Clients of `POST …/apply` must send `confirm` for changes marked `review.level = "elevated"`.
+
+## 1.0.0 — 2026-11-03
+Phases A–D, Phase T, Fix-with-agent, recipes, access token, readiness, retention. See git history.
